ions switch from $m\\times n$ to $n\\times m.$\n\nSo, since $P$ is a $6\\times 3$ matrix, the transpose ${P}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "f81a6da73d3e3f74ef632c0f1363da84c7a71db359dd65971cc6d083639d49a5"} {"question" "q-282786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "48e7decd4a6598f288c6775e9dcc29a21d7c37d9fcbf251eb9f4f98a97b403a8"} {"question" "q-282786" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "f81a6da73d3e3f74ef632c0f1363da84c7a71db359dd65971cc6d083639d49a5"} {"question" "q-282786" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "f81a6da73d3e3f74ef632c0f1363da84c7a71db359dd65971cc6d083639d49a5"} {"question" "q-282786" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "f81a6da73d3e3f74ef632c0f1363da84c7a71db359dd65971cc6d083639d49a5"} {"question" "q-282786" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "f81a6da73d3e3f74ef632c0f1363da84c7a71db359dd65971cc6d083639d49a5"} {"question" "q-70061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n    $D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of ${D}^{T}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "referen